---
import StudyLayout from "../../../layouts/StudyLayout.astro";

const review = {
	slug: "engine-effects-review",
	title: "Engine effects — study-quality evaluation",
	status: "exploratory" as const,
	phase: "integration" as const,
	question:
		"Study-quality assessment, 30 October 2026. Separate from feasibility and integration planning.",
};
---

<StudyLayout study={review}>
	<p><a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects">Return to the design study</a></p>
	<section aria-labelledby="readiness">
		<h2 id="readiness">Engine effects — study-quality evaluation</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Assessment: useful design conclusion, with evidence gaps.</strong>
			Review of sections 02.1–02.4, 30 October 2026. The plume lifecycle is
			accepted; the ribbon experiment remains unresolved. The owner wants no
			additional forward thrust at roughly 750 units/s. Exact taper, size
			mapping, and normal-scale readability still need review in flight.
		</p>
		<div class="review-table">
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col">Criterion</th>
						<th scope="col">Assessment</th>
						<th scope="col">Evidence and condition</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Purpose</th>
						<td>Supported</td>
						<td>
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#engine-purpose">01</a>
							establishes expressive, filled, glowing effects; the owner
							confirmed the visual direction in
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#plume-lifecycle">02.3</a>.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Investigation</th>
						<td>Supported</td>
						<td>
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#engine-direction">02.2</a>
							exposed ribbon cutoff and instant flame loss.
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#plume-lifecycle">02.3</a>
							supplied a reviewed alternative with one lifetime for the whole
							plume.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Alternatives and reasoning</th>
						<td>Supported</td>
						<td>
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#engine-next">02.1</a>,
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#engine-direction">02.2</a>,
							and
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#plume-lifecycle">02.3</a>
							preserve stamped residue, connected ribbon, and complete emitted
							surfaces. The last approach addresses release without a separate
							tail object.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Evidence fit</th>
						<td>Partial</td>
						<td>
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#plume-lifecycle">02.3</a>
							supports isolated motion and release, not arena readability.
							Before game adoption, inspect the fixed replay and live flight in
							the real Lab at each camera scale; revise if the effect obscures
							hazards or loses its character.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Cumulative agreement</th>
						<td>Supported</td>
						<td>
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#plume-lifecycle">02.3</a>
							records explicit lifecycle acceptance;
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#thrust-plume">02.4</a>
							records the approximate engine cutoff. Neither establishes
							acceptance of exact tuning or production delivery.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Design coherence</th>
						<td>Partial</td>
						<td>
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#thrust-plume">02.4</a>
							combines thrust-dependent size and fade in isolation. In the Lab
							trial, review turning, braking, both engines, release, cutoff,
							camera changes, wrapping, pause, and death/reset. Fix
							discontinuities before promotion.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Remaining uncertainty</th>
						<td>Partial</td>
						<td>
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#readiness"
								>Readiness questions</a
							>
							name the taper, visibility, and performance gaps. The owner
							reviews feel after the trial; measure performance on a named
							device before making a performance claim. Unresolved tuning
							remains provisional.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Integration implications</th>
						<td>Partial</td>
						<td>
							<a href="/lab/studies/engine-effects#integration"
								>Integration plan</a
							>
							maps the change to shared effects, physics, configuration, and the
							flight Lab. Verify that every engine's visual output uses its
							actual contribution and that physics and rendering tests pass
							before the experience review.
						</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p>
			This evaluates how well the study established purpose, investigated
			alternatives, preserved decisions, and produced a usable conclusion. The
			owner accepted the plume lifecycle and requested the approximate cutoff.
			Exact tuning and full-scene evidence remain incomplete; those limits are
			visible in parts 03 and 04.
		</p>
		<p>
			Human feedback also identified a process failure: the previous assessment
			confused study success with feasibility and implementation authorization.
			The corrected four-part structure separates these concerns. Its usefulness
			still requires human review; this record does not claim approval or
			delivery.
		</p>
	</section>
</StudyLayout>
<style>
.review-table {
	overflow-x: auto;
	margin-block: var(--spacing-lg);
}
table {
	width: 100%;
	border-collapse: collapse;
	font-size: var(--font-small);
}
th,
td {
	text-align: left;
	vertical-align: top;
	padding: var(--spacing-sm);
	border-bottom: var(--flight-border);
	line-height: 1.6;
}
th {
	color: var(--color-acid-lime);
}
</style>
